{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/625381-questions-on-mummy-the-resurection","id":625381,"title":"Questions on Mummy the Resurection...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-13T06:32:18-07:00","id":625381,"title":"Questions on Mummy the Resurection...","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> I'm thinking I've been pretty rough judging this game previously. Maybe due to my poor english I misunderstood something, but reading the manual some aspects have puzzeld me a little. Maybe you can explain them to me?<br /> <br /> 1) When a new Mummy is born, she's clearly just like a zombie, and need to travel to the middle-east to perform a ritual for a proper resurrection. It's correct? This implies that everyone which meet her during the journey can tell for sure that she's not human?<br /> <br /> 2) If a Mummy goes out of &quot;energy&quot; she need do go back in middle-east to charge herself? Then, if a scene is settled in Europe, a player which goes out of energy need to tell to his partners &quot;Sorry guys, I need to take a stroll in Egypt, I'll be back soon&quot;?<br /> <br /> 3) A silly question now: what happens if the two merging souls are male and female?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T08:52:31-07:00","id":625565,"title":"","content":"1) They can tell, but seeing a pre-ritual mummy triggers the Veil (MTR p. 80), causing human witnesses to freak out, much like the Delirium in Werewolf. One character in the Mummy Player's Guide bundled herself up in a thick coat to conceal what she was, although people still apparently stayed as far away as they could for whatever reason.<br /> <br /> 2) There are various ways to gain Sekhem; it's just easiest in the Middle East (MTR p. 144). Mummies automatically regain a point of Sekhem every day at sunrise no matter where they are. In addition, the Legacy and Vessel Backgrounds allow a mummy to replenish Sekhem; certain special places allow a mummy to meditate to regain Sekhem; the Udja-sen gain bonus Sekhem whenever they regain Sekhem and can share it with other mummies; mages can use Prime to grant Sekhem in the form of Quintessence; and there are certain Hekau that can provide Sekhem.<br /> <br /> Basically, a mummy outside of the Middle East should be advised to have some way of replenishing their Sekhem to hand if it looks like they'll run out.<br /> <br /> 3) That's up to player choice; it's raised as a possibility on p. 71 of the Mummy core in the Prelude section under &quot;Questions and Answers&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T12:52:39-07:00","id":625761,"title":"","content":"I see thanks for the explanation. Another question: after the fusion the two entities are one or they can still interact each other?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-13T13:25:18-07:00","id":625798,"title":"","content":"They're pretty much integrated (though it's not always seamless, as there's often a difference in worldview between the two souls). If they're not truly joined, they're very unlikely to successfully come through the Spell of Life (p. 23-24).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T00:43:43-07:00","id":626410,"title":"","content":"Well it is possible to regain there power outside the web of faith it is brutal and mechanically unlikely to work in most games, especially cross overs.<br /> <br /> It's usually something like spend a day mediating on a node make a diff 8 meditation roll if successful make a diff 9 power stat roll each success gives one point.<br /> <br /> It's seriously almost as bad as being a changeling","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T08:56:27-07:00","id":626696,"title":"","content":"Then setting chronicles outside the middle-east is pretty unseemly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-14T09:56:34-07:00","id":626718,"title":"","content":"No. As marin said, it's just easier, also bear in mind that's Egyptian Mummies. Caccophopian and Asian mummies as far as I can tell doesn't have that Web of Life affinity (for lack of a better term). In the Year of the Scarab trilogy, Nickolas Sforza-Ankhotep spent most of his time in either Chicago or New York, I forgot which it's been a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T03:34:43-07:00","id":627441,"title":"","content":"A question about the storyline According to the manual Osiris has kept a low profile for millennia and just recently he started to rise new mummies. My question is how much recent this recently is? Decades or maybe centuries?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T08:49:38-07:00","id":627639,"title":"","content":"Mummies have been around since the first edition in the WOD. The book you're referring to is the revised version and makes changes to the original template. So in the WOD the Mummies now after the 6th Great Malestrom are something new. The entire Web of Faith was originally a Mage thing that Osiris took over by virtue of insert choice here. Remember he also restored a number of Vampires to being humans at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-15T09:46:25-07:00","id":627673,"title":"","content":"At the time the MTR core was released, in 2001, Osiris had started raising new mummies since the Sixth Great Maelstrom began in 1999, a couple of years back. Assuming a modern day game, it'd now be 16 years back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-22T18:37:04-07:00","id":636528,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/625381-questions-on-mummy-the-resurection#post625381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1) When a new Mummy is born, she's clearly just like a zombie, and need to travel to the middle-east to perform a ritual for a proper resurrection. It's correct? This implies that everyone which meet her during the journey can tell for sure that she's not human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Per the core book (and the players guide), a number of the Reborn get to Egypt/the Middle East without attracting *too* much attention -- this is more so true for Ba and Ka aspect mummies, who have the ability to better understand and relate things via language (they may come across as very weird to people -- especially, of course, to those who knew them in their 2nd life -- but not &quot;OMG -- it's a zombie/undead thing!!!&quot;. Sahu mummies tend to &quot;luck&quot; their way towards their goals, with happenstance helping them in minor ways; this is somewhat the same case with Khu, but they are the least &quot;sentient&quot; of the soul-aspects, at least by conventional standards. Khaibit, however, on the other hand... &quot;CNN UPDATE: a plane that was hijacked from out of BWI-airport, near Washington DC, has crashed near Cairo, Egypt... no reported survivors...&quot; (... with reports of some rampaging beast coming up out of the wreckage being discounted as mass-hysteria...). It *can* be tricky for some mummies, but the majority of them the Completing Spirit can muddle it's way through things to get to a resurrection cult without *too* much crazy shit going on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/625381-questions-on-mummy-the-resurection#post625381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 2) If a Mummy goes out of &quot;energy&quot; she need do go back in middle-east to charge herself? Then, if a scene is settled in Europe, a player which goes out of energy need to tell to his partners &quot;Sorry guys, I need to take a stroll in Egypt, I'll be back soon&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are referring to Semektet (the weakening that occurs when most mummies drop to 0 Sekhem), then yes, the rules say that they have to make a journey back to The Web of Faith to give themselves a &quot;jump start&quot;, as it were, to get their &quot;battery&quot; running again. After that, though, they can travel again (often within just a day of arriving), so long as they don't deplete themselves again (that is, don't let themselves drop down to 0, using their daily recovery to slowly rebuild power again).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/625381-questions-on-mummy-the-resurection#post625381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> 3) A silly question now: what happens if the two merging souls are male and female?</div> </div> </div> </div>This happens for a good proportion of the uniting spirit-shards (the First and Second lives are often enough of different genders). It's not really that complicated -- they merge just as any spirit shards might. The Second Life is still the mostly dominant person, in terms of personality, with the Completing Spirit adding perhaps a few traits of its own (this is conceptually similar to -- if you've ever watched the show -- Deep Space Nine, where some Trill are combined with a symbiotic alien that melds with their personality to create a somewhat new persona). It's a change, sometimes somewhat minor overall, sometimes very significant/major, but in most situations the new mummy has most of the same recognizable personality traits, with a few new ones added. Otherwise, though, the genders don't really matter -- it's not as significant as you might think for most cases.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have been around here for waaaayyyy too fucking long...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1433-just-john-forever","name":"Just John, Forever...","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T04:19:09-07:00","id":636874,"title":"","content":"This is why I kinda prefer the Mummies prior to Resurrection :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-23T10:18:25-07:00","id":637146,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/625381-questions-on-mummy-the-resurection?p=636874#post636874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is why I kinda prefer the Mummies prior to Resurrection :P</div> </div> </div> </div>Me too. Also, there's a problem with the oWoD in that changelings, demons and mummies are all either humans with a bit of something else's soul or a supernatural spirit with a bit of a human soul to give it personality and memories. Arguably, even mages and fera fit this description too.<br /> <br /> For me, it began to feel like a 'one-size-fits-all' approach to playing monsters, where the human part of the being means you're still pretty much playing something understandable through a human lens. It'd be nice to actually play something completely inhuman for once, and with a unique way of coming into being. The 'merged/united soul' thing became a crutch, in that it stopped you from actually playing monsters, but meant you were actually playing humans plus.<br /> <br /> Mummies, especially, don't particularly fit the 'part human, part monster' model too well. It was better (for me) when they were humans so divorced from everyday existence that they'd become monsters.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's a minor rant, really. I otherwise like MTR. I just wish they'd been the original mummies, instead of the fragments of the original mummies fused with a regular person from now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T15:18:12-07:00","id":638402,"title":"","content":"Just read up on sekhem recovery and it's as bad as I remember. Legacy background is great but requires you be in a very specific location related to you history. Mages can help if they have the quintessence to spare. <br /> <br /> Vessel is useful for a limited time but can only be recovered in the web if Faith. There are a few spells that let you store it if you have it but won't be much good unless you have it to spare.<br /> <br /> You get one a day for free but aside from that you need to meditate. Meditate on a node for a full day and make a meditation roll dif 8 if successful it takes a further balance roll dif 9 to recover anything. A starting mummy with balance 3 and a 7 pool meditation on average will spend 24 hours meditating to get nothing.<br /> <br /> Long story short out side the middle east a mummy better have lots of resources to cover there regular trips back and forth.<br /> <br /> It dose not help that most of there magic cost sekhem making them only slightly better than mortal most of the time and similar to sorcerers the rest of the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2939-avaron","name":"Avaron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2939_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}